    "body": "**Raised to P0** - confirmed: on a mill-turn the cross drill posted silently with its rapids 5 mm inside uncut raw stock (r10 bar in r20 stock: start/approach at r15, station-change rapid `G00 X21.213 Y0 Z10 -> G00 X0 Y21.213 Z0` passing r15). The verification gate returned no warnings because the rapid-in-stock check is off for radial drilling (Mode::Radial).\n\nFix landed locally on issue/77-cross-drill-raw-stock (08da1b3, stacked on #67 / PR #78), gating now:\n- new `operation/cross_stock.rs`: stand off the larger of the part and the setup stock about the same spindle (box stock at its circumscribed radius, cylinder at its radius); hole mouths move out to the raw surface, bottoms unchanged; the stock's Z top sets the over-the-end-face route;\n- every rapid is proved against stock radius + drill half-width (or above the stock top), refused by name otherwise;\n- stock == part or no stock: bit-identical to before;\n- resizing the stock now stales the cross drill (before, the old hops would post).\nAfter: start, approach and station-change rapids all at r25. Tests: drilling_cross_stock (4).",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
