    "body": "Review fixes landed locally (9d0527a): an off-centre hole's mouth is placed where the drill's edge nearest the axis meets the raw surface, and the proof checks the drill's full width (and a wider shank) down the hole line - the edge at the approach's end moved from r19.792 (inside the r20 bar) to r20.956; the end-face swing clears max(d, shank)/2 (3 mm drill on a 6 mm shank: swing z 21.6 -> 23.1 over the z20 face); a hole pointing away from the spindle is refused by name; the end-face check runs first (the old proof refused every raw-stock opposite pair). Tests: drilling_cross_stock 8 (4 new). Holder sweep on the swing -> #84.",
